        "id": 3758334
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-20T03:00:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ArrayLengthFromUniform choose to issue vec4\u003cu32\u003e to store buffer lengths.\nMy thoughts:\n- To make padding easy.\n- ArrayLengthFromUniform is a general transform, which means hlsl backend requires it too.And in hlsl backend, all uniform contents will be transferred into vec4. However, it is possible to keep u32s array and then apply transform to convert it into vec4 in hlsl.\n\njrprice@ do you know the exact reason?",
      "parentUuid": "5f0687e0_e2e6fd7a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 330,
        "startChar": 90,
        "endLine": 331,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "29776d7886d27000efdc7933d144bae7d0891fce",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
